# Code owners.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the Tier 1 block below replaces the default
# owners for those paths rather than adding to them.
#
# This file does nothing until branch protection on `main` and `release/*` turns
# on "Require review from Code Owners". The recommended settings are in
# docs/postmortems/20261021-data-loss-and-process-failures.md, "Branch
# protection". A caveat from there: GitHub never lets an account approve its own
# PR. While every PR is opened from the account listed below, a code-owner
# review on a Tier 1 path cannot be given. Open PRs from a separate machine
# account first, or the rule will be bypassed and mean nothing.

# Default.
*                                   @ConduitIO/conduit-core @devarismeroxa

# Tier 1 (CLAUDE.md, "PR review process"): record flow, ack/position/checkpoint
# logic, state, connector protocol, serialization formats. Human sign-off by
# DeVaris is required; the default owners are not enough.
